COPY public.business_value (id, title, description, release_id) FROM stdin;
99ab8c26-7905-4462-9f32-da7675967559	FF! Plugins and FF! Components	We've added the ability to allow endusers to further customize their FrankApplication where different types of components can be (dynamically) added to the Frank!Application. Think of custom Java code, changing loggers, entire configurations, parts of configurations, or custom pipes.\n\nBecause of this users can create reusable configuration snippets, create their own custom FrankElements and even hook into the Framework's lifecycle.\n\nIn order to accomodate this we've added a new property expression language. This allows users to dynamically change or use code-snippets, frank-elements or set property values.\n\nWe've also added new FrankElements such as:\n- ConfigWarning\n- PipelinePart\n- CompositeSender\n- CompositePipe	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4SsUJ7
d46ad16d-c3e0-4f89-9233-896aad8bb574	OpenAPI validation	We've extended our JSON schema validators so they can now also use an OpenAPI schema to validate the input and output of listeners/senders.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4SsUJ7
4f9ebb7a-2c4b-4bbb-8ebc-f022fbaa0563	Drivers have been removed from our base images	As end-users want to be in control which driver version is used. So they can easily be upgraded when needed without changing the application layer, we've created a separate classpath for drivers. This new classpath can be found at `/opt/frank/drivers` so drivers can be mounted easily. API specifications such as the Jakarta transaction-api and messaging-api's are on the application server's default classpath. As they are an integral part of the Frank!Framework Application they should not be overridden or removed.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
ddc5c1aa-7cb0-4c04-9dde-471f777f521f	Enhanced SCM and faster CVE resolutions	We've improved our Supply Chain by, in a controlled manner, automatically merging new dependency versions.\nOlder releases have been moved to our 'cold' archive, and are no longer pubicly accessable. New releases will still be available on DockerHub and our Nexus. Dependencies are automatically merged after a week cooldown unless they are marked as a CVE fix. As usual, nightlies can be found on our GitHub Releases page as well as here on the FF! "user". We aim to further automate the patch-version release pipelines to publish our artifacts on Central.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4SsUJ7
745afdce-b90d-46c6-82fa-74364e80778e	Adapter Flow image improvements	In order to further futureproof our AdapterFlow images we've started to migrate away from Mermaid and are using our own placing algorithm.\n\nWe're also working on a new graphical designer and are working towards a way to display thumbnails of the designed flow opposed to a generated one.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4SsUJ7
a44994f9-3cf1-4e36-9a83-36eaf3d3c271	Improvements on the BearerOnly Authentication flow	It is now possible to not only validate but also authenticate users in combination with the BearerOnly authenticator. The JWT will be validated againt the JWKS provided.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
637a5b66-b284-4bda-87c5-3538d4d24c78	Major JVM and dependency bumps	The Java Runtime has been upgraded from 17 to 21.\nThe Spring Framework has been upgraded from 6 to 7.\nThe Angular has been upgraded from 20 to 21.\nAdd support for Kubernetes v1.33	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
0e27d39c-86c5-4108-bb68-1aa5d7ddd233	Improved the Kubernetes capability	The Kubernetes capability has been added to our base image allowing end-users to use their Frank!Application more easily on their Kubernetes platform.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
ec3b24d8-56aa-4464-8202-61ef933b0e73	JSON and DataSonnet improvements	We've worked hard on improving our JSON support. Both processing and transforming capabilities have been given a facelift.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
6804dbd1-84ca-4231-afc9-f72bef7993f1	CredentialProvider has been added to the FF! Console	In order to securely connect to a backend system (database) the 'CredentialProvider' and 'Kubernetes' Frank!Framework capabilities have been added to the FF! Console.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4Q-1RU
314d6429-a55a-4525-8cbd-a54f1f5a102a	Larva and stubbing improvements	We are giving our Larva testtool an overhaul to allow users to more easily test their integration flows, make the tool less error-prone to use and make the tooling more configurable so it fits everyones testing needs.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4QXRm4
683fba22-e3a3-43f5-8aae-5635839e1c4c	CredentialProvider has been added to the FF! Console	In order to securely connect to a backend system (database) the 'CredentialProvider' and 'Kubernetes' Frank!Framework capabilities have been added to the FF! Console.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4QXRm4
281b10e3-d99b-4b64-bc42-145ed390f2e7	JSON and DataSonnet improvements	We've worked hard on improving our JSON support. Both processing and transforming capabilities have been given a facelift.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4QXRm4
d954d199-aa4c-4204-aa4b-9030c8d71430	Add Expression Language for properties	We've added the new capability to use properly expressions so values can be determined based on external factors.\n\nAs such it's now possible to set the `active` attribute based on the presence of a property, give custom `ConfigurationWarnings` when properties or attributes have not been set. This allows the usage of expressions in property values, such as `${value}.isEmpty()`.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4QXRm4
0510cba8-ae4a-4a88-91ab-2a3c983ae809	Cache and Keystore element improvements	We've kicked off our Epic to improve and rework certain Cache settings to further improve it's use. We've also introduced a new Keystore element, designed for the specific keystore attributes, so they no longer clutter the pipes/sender they are on.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4VMw66
3a59b1bc-ab4a-4cd4-87d4-ad103cbc12ba	Performance Improvements	Less memory required for simple find/replace tasks and the Aspose module is fully streaming. We've also made steps to improve WebService throughput as an opt-in, you will need to configure `WebServiceListener.cxfServlet=false` in order to use the new non-cxf based soap RPC endpoints.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4VMw66
280a0b21-4dd8-4fe1-a1a0-5c5e29459793	Log output improvements	We've changed log levels of individual loggers, and simplified the log output when running containerized instances.\nThe standard out should produce a more human readable log output.\nException traces have been normalized (where possible).	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4VMw66
92ca6141-240f-4e54-a1d1-df20f828cad0	SOAP improvements	We've implemented the SOAP Addressing standard, allowing end users to specify a messageID as well as 'response-id' in the SOAPHeader.\n\nWe've also made steps to improve WebService throughput as an opt-in, you will need to configure `WebServiceListener.cxfServlet=false` in order to use the new non-cxf based soap RPC endpoints.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4VMw66
386bf0af-d5b7-4a83-ab0a-3513d3a101be	Console QoL	Quality of life improvements for certain pages such as test-pipeline, adapter status and the message- and error-storages.	RE_kwDOAIg5ds4VMw66
\.
